# Rust invariants

## Paths and persistence

- Runtime files: `get_data_dir().join(...)` — never hardcode `/data` or relative paths
- Persist with atomic write + rename (see `ping.rs`, memory, flight tracker)
- Embedded CSVs via `include_str!` in `data/` — no runtime file deps for prod image

## Time

- All time ops use `Europe/Berlin` (see `.cargo/config.toml` timezone filter)

## Config security

- Config structs: `Deserialize` only — **never** add `Serialize` (credential leak via debug dump)
- Secrets in `SecretString` (secrecy crate)

## IRC / handlers

- Handlers are independent; errors in one must not crash others (`bail!` on startup only)
- Broadcast channel capacity 100; lagging handlers continue after `RecvError::Lagged`
- Request/response on broadcast: subscribe **before** send (PING/PONG race)
- `twitch_irc::irc!` macro needs standalone `use twitch_irc::irc;`

## Resilience

- Aviation client init failure: log, disable aviation features — do not abort the bot
- Ping templates: reject control chars on create/edit (CR/LF splits PRIVMSG)

## Style

- Clippy is strict (`-D warnings`); don't `#[allow]` without a one-line reason
- Log errors with `?error` not `%error` (includes backtrace)
